"""Wires tracing and metrics: the tracer provider, the exporter, the metric
registry, and the process-level metrics every service publishes.

Belongs here: provider construction and shutdown, exporter configuration,
metric definitions and their label sets.

Does NOT belong here: the middleware that records a span or observes a request
duration — that is transport-specific and lives in
`internal/transport/http`. This package hands out the instruments; it does not
know what an HTTP request is.

The one rule worth stating twice: never label a metric with an unbounded
value. No user IDs, no raw paths, no error strings. A route template is a
label; a URL is not.

Empty until Mint chunk 08.
"""
